nodes.goal:
Preflight the release lane BEFORE any change: {run.project_dir}
Target version: {run.version}
Run from that directory:
1. git status --short and git rev-parse --abbrev-ref HEAD - the lane must be clean and on the branch you are releasing from; a dirty tree or detached branch is a HALT condition (proceed=false), never stashed away silently.
2. Consistency now: {run.check_command} - record the exact output. If it fails, note WHICH files drift and compare the versions present against BOTH the last tag (git describe --tags --abbrev=0) and the target: a tree where some files already read {run.version} and others do not is a HALF-DONE RELEASE - proceed=false with half_done=true so a human repairs it; re-running the bump over it can be a no-op.
3. Changelog sanity: is there an entry for {run.version} (or an Unreleased section), and are there commits since the last tag the changelog does not mention?
Reply with ONLY fenced json {"clean_tree": true|false, "branch": "<name>", "check_output": "<verbatim tail>", "half_done": true|false, "drift_files": ["<path or note>"], "changelog_ready": true|false, "proceed": true|false, "why": "<one paragraph citing the commands>"}
proceed MUST be false if the tree is dirty, the check fails for any reason other than 'the target version simply is not bumped yet' (that alone is normal pre-prep state), or a half-done release is detected.

Verify publication on ONE channel by running ITS OWN check - the pipeline going green does not prove a specific channel received the artifact.
Channel: {channel}
Check command: {check}
Run it. live=true ONLY on exit 0 with output that actually names the expected version; a check that cannot run is live=false with the error, never a guess. Work only this channel.

Write the release closeout from the machine records auto-injected in ## Inputs - not from prose claims. Read the fan-out's all_results: every channel the intake listed must appear ANSWERED (live true/false with evidence) or be NAMED missing; count against the intake's list, do not assume it.
If your inputs show halt-notice or drift-halt as the live arm, the release did NOT publish: report published=false and the halt reason; state plainly which arm ran. Otherwise report the tag/ref from the publish node's output, the gate answer from the approve record, and one line per channel: name, live verdict, evidence.
Reply with ONLY fenced json {"published": true|false, "ref": "<tag or empty>", "channels": ["<name>: live|missing|failed - <evidence tail>"], "dispatched": <int>, "answered": <int>, "missing": ["<channel>"], "verdict": "released|halted|incomplete"}
